---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<Legal
	title="App Terms"
	description="Additional terms for OAuth applications built by Eric Boothe, such as ebrain-hermes, which access only his own Google account data."
	label="apps"
	updated="2026-09-18"
>
	<p>
		In addition to the site <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Use</a> and
		<a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, these terms apply to OAuth
		applications published by Eric Boothe, including
		<code>ebrain-hermes</code> and any similar apps registered under this
		domain.
	</p>

	<h2>What these apps are</h2>
	<p>
		They are personal automation tools. Each app requests access to Google
		account data (for example Gmail, Calendar, or Drive) solely so that I can
		automate tasks on <strong>my own</strong> Google account. They are not a
		service offered to the public, are not monetized, and are not intended to
		be authorized by anyone other than me.
	</p>

	<h2>Who should authorize them</h2>
	<p>
		<strong>If you are not Eric Boothe, you should not authorize these
		applications.</strong> They will not do anything useful for you, and any
		access you grant will be revoked as soon as it is noticed. You can revoke
		access at any time from your
		<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google account permissions page</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>How data is handled</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Data is accessed only to perform the automation the app was built for.</li>
		<li>It is not sold, shared with third parties, or used for advertising.</li>
		<li>Retention is limited to what the automation needs; nothing is kept for its own sake.</li>
		<li>
			Use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
			<a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
			including the Limited Use requirements.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Everything else about data handling is covered by the
		<a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>No warranty</h2>
	<p>
		These apps are provided as-is for personal use. They may change or be
		discontinued at any time without notice.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about any of these applications can be sent to
		<a href="mailto:ericboothe@gmail.com">ericboothe@gmail.com</a>.
	</p>
</Legal>
